  "text_md": "133 STAT. 1072 PUBLIC LAW 116–49—AUG. 22, 2019\n\n## Public Law 116–49 116th Congress\n\n## An Act\n\n<u>Aug. 22, 2019</u> To amend the Public Health Service Act to reauthorize the Emergency Medical [H.R. 776] Services for Children program.\n\n*Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of* Emergency *the United States of America in Congress assembled,* Medical Services for Children **SECTION 1. SHORT TITLE.** Program This Act may be cited as the ‘‘Emergency Medical Services Reauthorization Act of 2019.for Children Program Reauthorization Act of 2019’’. 42 USC 201 note. **SEC. 2. REAUTHORIZATION OF THE EMERGENCY MEDICAL SERVICES** **FOR CHILDREN PROGRAM.** Section 1910(d) of the Public Health Service Act (42 U.S.C. 300w–9(d)) is amended—\n\n(1) by striking ‘‘2014, and’’ and inserting ‘‘2014,’’; and\n(2) by inserting before the period the following: ‘‘, and\n$22,334,000 for each of fiscal years 2020 through 2024’’.\n\n### Approved August 22, 2019.\n\n<u>LEGISLATIVE</u> HISTORY—H.R. 776 (S. 1173): HOUSE REPORTS: No. 116–176 (Comm. on Energy and Commerce). CONGRESSIONAL RECORD, Vol. 165 (2019): July 24, considered and passed House. July 31, considered and passed Senate.\n\nÆ\n\ndkrause on DSKBC28HB2PROD with PUBLAWS VerDate Sep 11 2014 10:09 Aug 26, 2019 Jkt 089139 PO 00049 Frm 00001 Fmt 6580 Sfmt 6580 E:\\PUBLAW\\PUBL049.116 PUBL049\n",
